\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1.   From the Eastern mountains
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0   Pressing on they come,
\par   Wise men in their wisdom,
\par   To His humble home,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   Stirred by deep devotion,
\par   Hasting from afar,
\par   Ever journeying onward,
\par   Guided by a star.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.   There their Lord and Saviour
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0   Meek and lowly lay,
\par   Wondrous light that led them
\par   Onward on their way,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6   Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Ever now to lighten
\par    Nations from afar,
\par   As they journey homeward
\par   By that guiding star.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  Thou who in a manger
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0   Once hast lowly lain,
\par   Who dost now in glory
\par   O'er all kingdoms reign,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Gather in the heathen,
\par  Who in lands afar
\par  Ne'er have seen the brightness
\par  Of Thy guiding star.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   4.  Gather in the outcasts,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  All who have gone astray,
\par  Throw Thy radiance o'er them,
\par  Guide them on their way,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6   Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Those who never knew Thee,
\par  Those who have wandered far,
\par    Guide them by the brightness
\par  Of Thy guiding star.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  Onward through the darkness
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0   Of the lonely night,
\par  Shining still before them
\par  With Thy kindly light,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Guide them, Jew and Gentile,
\par  Homeward from afar,
\par  Young and old together,
\par \pard      By Thy guiding star.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

